From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:29:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] [VideoPlayer] DRM PRIME: standard Dolby Vision through
 libpi_engine

Standard (TV-led) Dolby Vision needs the source to reshape each picture
with its RPU (and enhancement layer) into the 12-bit signal the sink
expects, tunnelled in 8-bit RGB frames. On the Raspberry Pi 5 the
libpi_engine library does that on the GPU (Vulkan), from the DRM PRIME
frames the V4L2 request decoder exports and the RPU side data FFmpeg
attaches.

When Kodi is built with it (the optional PiDV dependency, pkg-config
pi_engine), CRendererDRMPRIME renders Dolby Vision profile 5, 7 and 8
pictures into tunnel frames and puts those on the video plane, fenced,
with the connector set for standard Dolby Vision. It does so where the
display reports Dolby Vision and "Allowed HDR dynamic metadata formats"
includes it, a setting now offered on GBM builds with the engine.
Otherwise, or if the mode isn't the stream's size, playback is as
before.

Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
